Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 4.4  Permutation null test. Grey histograms: the latitude span of \
the monthly centroid loop under 500 random month-label shufflings (locations \
kept, the month\[Dash]location link broken). Coloured line: the observed span \
(Arctic tern ",
 "110.8",
 "\[Degree], common swift ",
 "63.6",
 "\[Degree], red knot ",
 "33.6",
 "\[Degree]). Every observed span is five to seven times the largest shuffled \
value (and seven to ten times the average shuffle; ",
 StyleBox["p < 0.002",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", n = 500) \[LongDash] the seasonal loop is a real signal in the data, not \
an artifact of a static, seasonally-mislabelled range."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"762c8ec1-f33f-4629-ae3d-163467743c1a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Robustness check \[LongDash] how sharply is each monthly centroid pinned?\
\>", "Subsection",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"542545fd-1c08-4cfc-af16-74150f06006e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A point on a map invites false confidence. Each monthly centroid is an \
estimate from a finite, uneven sample, so it deserves an error bar. We attach \
one by ",
 StyleBox["block-bootstrapping over years",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ": for each month we resample the 2014\[Dash]2024 years with replacement, \
recompute the gridded centroid, repeat 300 times, and draw the 95% confidence \
ellipse of the resulting cloud. Tight ellipses mark well-sampled months; \
sprawling ones mark the sparse, oceanic stretches where the centroid is \
barely constrained."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"23976534-5735-489d-8c4d-814baf5da4a8"],

